soft.com/category/windows/blog/sysinternals-blog"},{"DocumentLabel":"Sysinternals Resources","DocumentUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/resources/"},{"DocumentLabel":"Sysinternals Utilities Index","DocumentUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/"},{"DocumentLabel":"Troubleshooting with the Windows Sysinternals Tools","DocumentUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/resources/troubleshooting-book"}],"license":"Proprietary","licenseUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/license-terms","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"There are several applications, such as service packs and hotfixes, that must replace a file that's in use and is unable to. Windows therefore provides the MoveFileEx API to rename or delete a file and allows the caller to specify that they want the operation to take place the next time the system boots,before the files are referenced. Session Manager performs this task by reading the registered rename and delete commands from the HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager\\PendingFileRenameOperations value.\n\nMoveFile usage:\nThe included MoveFile utility allows you to schedule move and delete commands for the next reboot: \nusage: movefile [source] [dest]","moniker":"movefile","name":"MoveFile","packageUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/pendmoves","privacyUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/license-terms","publisher":"Sysinternals","publisherSupportUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/answers/tags/435/sysinternals","publisherUrl":"https://www.sysinternals.com/","tags":["sysinternals"]}},"publisherSupportUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/answers/tags/435/sysinternals","publisherUrl":"https://www.sysinternals.com/","releaseDate":"2026-11-11","releaseDateSource":"commit","schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","upstream":{"commit":"411ee5b30152224ab652f0629684a360adabd366","manifestVersion":"1.12.0","manifests":[{"path"